Usage: updatedb [OPTION]...

Update the filename database used by locate.
Walks the filesystem and writes a sorted path list.
The database is written to a temporary file and renamed
into place, replacing any previous database atomically.
Database entries are plain path lines (a Windows platform
deviation from GNU LOCATE02).

OPTIONS:
  -d, --directory ARG    directory to start walking
  -e, --exclude ARG      prune entries whose path contains this pattern
  -f                     accepted for compatibility; ignored
      --localpaths ARG   walk these roots (semicolon separated) instead of
                         --directory
  -o, --output ARG       database output file
      --prunepaths ARG   directories (semicolon separated) not to descend into
  -s                     accepted for compatibility; ignored
  -v, --verbose          be verbose
  -x, --exclude-dir ARG  directory name pattern to exclude
      --help             display this help and exit
  -V, --version          output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
